pixelshorts takes ideas from two MIT-licensed projects. No code or assets were copied from them.
Reference frames, music and templates from those projects are not included here.

claude-animated-shorts, https://github.com/mromidev/claude-animated-shorts
Copyright (c) 2026 Mr omi. MIT License.
Used for: the script formula, the 3.7 words per second pace, the 55 to 70 second target,
synthesized score and SFX on one beat table, and the idea of a frame-by-frame QA check.

pixel-plays, https://github.com/amirmushichge/pixel-plays
Copyright (c) 2026 Amir Mushich. MIT License. Its music is under other terms and is not used.
Used for: the look. Low-resolution frame, nearest-neighbour upscale, fixed isometric camera,
Bayer dither, hue-shifted colour ramps, long cast shadows, a dithered edge dissolving into the background.

The bitmap font follows the common 5x7 layout, also found in Adafruit-GFX (BSD).
